Package: swaydesk-widgets
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-scripts (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: wireplumber, pulseaudio-utils, network-manager, bluez, upower, cliphist, wl-clipboard, fonts-noto-color-emoji
Description: Sway desktop components - Waybar popups and icons
 Popups for the Waybar modules (calendar, weather, battery, audio,
 brightness, caffeine, network, Bluetooth, system, media and clipboard),
 the icons for weather, network, Bluetooth and system, and the on-screen
 volume and brightness indicator.

Package: swaydesk-capture
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-scripts (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: grim, slurp, wf-recorder, jq, wl-clipboard, libnotify-bin
Description: Sway desktop components - screenshot and screen recording panels
 The screenshot and screen recording panels (region, full screen or
 window, with delay, Gradia and audio options) over a dimmed screen.

Package: swaydesk-theme
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libglib2.0-bin
Recommends: papirus-icon-theme, dconf-cli, gnome-themes-extra
Description: Sway desktop components - theme tools, accent portal and Displays
 sway-theme and sway-desktop-config: the GTK theme, icons and accent
 color across the desktop, with the Papirus folder colors, and an
 org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Settings backend that gives the accent color
 to libadwaita apps. The Desktop Theme app picks the theme family, light or
 dark style and color with a live preview.
 .
 The Displays app arranges the screens (position, resolution, refresh
 rate, scale and rotation), and its service applies the layout saved for
 each set of monitors when they are plugged in or out.

Package: swaydesk-session
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-scripts (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, libpam0g, python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtksessionlock-0.1, gtklock
Description: Sway desktop components - session menu, lock screen and services
 The full-screen session menu (lock, log out, suspend, reboot, power
 off), a minimal org.gnome.SessionManager for Sway (reboot and shutdown
 for GNOME Software updates) and the first-login keyring fix for
 gnome-keyring.
 .
 The lock screen (swaydesk-lock) uses ext-session-lock through
 gtk4-layer-shell 1.2 or newer. It checks the password with its own PAM
 service (/etc/pam.d/swaydesk-lock, the same "auth include login" as
 swaylock's), loading libpam at run time. Where gtk4-layer-shell is older
 (Debian 13), the lock is sway-lock-gtk, the same lock in Python with GTK 3
 and gtk-session-lock. gtklock is the fallback locker; swaylock is no
 longer used, since it takes no dead keys.

Package: swaydesk-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-scripts (= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-notifd (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-notifd (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-dock (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-dock (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-drawer (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-drawer (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-widgets (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-widgets (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-capture (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-capture (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-theme (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-theme (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-session (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-session (<< ${source:Version}.1~), swaydesk-efi (>= ${source:Version}), swaydesk-efi (<< ${source:Version}.1~), ${misc:Depends}, sway, swaybg, swayidle, waybar, kitty, rofi, qalc, jq, curl, wl-clipboard, cliphist, xdg-desktop-portal-wlr, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, dconf-cli, libglib2.0-bin, fonts-noto-core, fonts-noto-color-emoji, gnome-themes-extra, adw-gtk-theme, systemd, mate-polkit | lxpolkit
Recommends: papirus-icon-theme, thunar | file-manager, grim, slurp, wf-recorder, brightnessctl, playerctl, pavucontrol, gammastep, blueman, network-manager-applet | network-manager-gnome, libnotify-bin, power-profiles-daemon, xwayland, qt5ct, qt6ct, gnome-text-editor
Suggests: fcitx5
Description: Sway desktop - the full session
 The "Sway Desktop" session for the display manager: the Sway and Waybar
 configuration, the session scripts and the first-login setup, using
 only the swaydesk components. It sits beside any session that the
 repository's install.sh sets up, and shares the user's settings
 (colors, fonts, keyboard, wallpaper) with it.
 .
 Alt+Space opens rofi. On Debian 13, rofi 1.7 runs through Xwayland
 (recommended). qalc powers the calculator of the app grid.
 .
 Not in the Debian archive, and optional: the Bibata cursor.

Package: swaydesk-greeter
Architecture: any
Depends: swaydesk-common (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, greetd, sway
Recommends: libpam-gnome-keyring
Description: Sway desktop - login screen for greetd
 A graphical login screen in GTK 4, in the look of the Sway desktop lock
 screen: the account list with AccountsService photos, the password and
 any further PAM question (a code, an expired password), the session
 list from wayland-sessions with the last one remembered, the system
 keyboard layout and language, and suspend, restart and shut down.
 .
 It runs in its own Sway, opened by greetd through a drop-in for
 greetd.service; /etc/greetd/config.toml is left untouched. greetd turns
 itself on when no other display manager is set; otherwise
 "systemctl enable greetd" after disabling the current one switches to it.
 A greeter already set in /etc/greetd/config.toml is replaced; to keep it
 without removing this package, mask the drop-in:
 "sudo mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d && sudo ln -s
 /dev/null /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d/swaydesk-greeter.conf &&
 sudo systemctl daemon-reload", effective at the next boot.

Package: swaydesk-efi
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: shim-signed
Description: Sway desktop - EFI fallback path of the Swaydesk ISO installs
 Only acts on a system installed from a Swaydesk ISO; on any other system,
 including a Debian or Ubuntu that only added the Swaydesk repository, it
 does nothing at all.
 .
 On a Swaydesk ISO install, it keeps the firmware's fallback boot path
 (EFI/BOOT) a working copy of the Swaydesk folder (EFI/swaydesk) under
 Secure Boot: shim with GRUB and MokManager next to it, the fallback
 loader that creates the boot entry again after it was lost (a firmware
 reset, the disk in another computer), the GRUB configuration stub, and
 the entry name "swaydesk" in shim's list. APT runs it after every package
 change, since the GRUB and shim upgrades redo that path; it also fixes
 the installs from the 0.1.3 ISOs, whose fallback path Secure Boot refuses.
 .
 It never touches the boot entries in NVRAM, the other systems' folders or
 a fallback path that belongs to another system, and it never fails APT.
 On an Ubuntu install from a 0.1.3 image, it renames the old
 EFI/ubuntu/BOOTX64.CSV that names the entry "Swaydesk" (to
 BOOTX64.CSV.swaydesk-old), so the firmware gets a single Swaydesk entry
 back.
 Changes go to the journal (swaydesk-efi). To turn it off, write "off" to
 /etc/swaydesk/efi-fallback.
